courses.learning_outcomes:
Upon completion of the subject, students will be able to:
1) apply substantial knowledge of new developments in global political economy, and incorporate it into their understanding of more traditional or long-standing GPE concerns;
2) identify contrasting perspectives on these new developments, and the evidentiary base on which they are founded;
3) analyse future developments in the same issue area with depth and sophistication, drawing upon the foundational knowledge imparted in this course.

Upon completion of this course, students will be able to:

1) Acquire knowledge of the relationship between Hong Kong, Macao and mainland China;
2) Analyze the significance of Hong Kong and Macao in furthering China's foreign interests;
3) Explore future developments in Hong Kong-Mainland relations and Macao-Mainland relations; and

4) Reflect upon the significance of such freedom in furthering the interests of the Greater China Region to the uniqueness of Hong Kong and Macao
